{"ref":"BDB, אֶשְׁכֹּל","hw":"אֶשְׁכֹּל","html":"† <big><span dir=\"rtl\">אֶשְׁכֹּל</span></big>  <strong>n.pr. </strong><br><strong>1.</strong>  <strong> m.</strong> an Amorite, brother of Mamre, dwelling in neighbourhood of Hebron <a data-ref=\"Genesis 14:13\" href=\"/Genesis.14.13\">Gn 14:13</a>, <a data-ref=\"Genesis 14:24\" href=\"/Genesis.14.24\">24</a>.<br><strong>2.</strong>  in combination <span dir=\"rtl\">נַחַל אֶשְׁכֹּל</span> <a data-ref=\"Numbers 13:23\" href=\"/Numbers.13.23\">Nu 13:23</a> <a data-ref=\"Deuteronomy 1:24\" href=\"/Deuteronomy.1.24\">Dt 1:24</a>; <span dir=\"rtl\">נ׳ אֶשְׁכּוֹל</span> <a data-ref=\"Numbers 13:24\" href=\"/Numbers.13.24\">Nu 13:24</a>, <a data-ref=\"Numbers 32:9\" href=\"/Numbers.32.9\">32:9</a>;—<em>valley of Eshcol</em>, = <em>valley of a cluster</em>, region of Hebron (cf. <a data-ref=\"Numbers 13:22\" href=\"/Numbers.13.22\">13:22</a>); in <a data-ref=\"Numbers 13:24\" href=\"/Numbers.13.24\">13:24</a> der. from <span dir=\"rtl\">א׳</span> <em>cluster</em>, q.v.; see however Di <em>ad loc.</em>","next":"BDB, אַשְׁכְּנַז","prev":"BDB, אֶשְׁכּוֹל"}